{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: publish what is at 655bef02 and get it reviewed. This replaces b5bf2e4e, whose central premise I confirmed is false.\n\nI CHECKED YOUR RETRACTION RATHER THAN ACCEPTING IT. TestLocalMarkdownLinks at public_surface_test.go:121 resolves its own path through runtime.Caller(0) and walks from the module root, skipping only .git, .tmp and node_modules, and it fails on both missing link targets and missing heading anchors. git log -S dates it to 35331448 on 2026-08-09, a fortnight before I filed the request. README.md has been gated the whole time. So has every other markdown file in the tree.\n\nYOUR ARGUMENT AGAINST EXTENDING THE DOCSET WALKER IS ACCEPTED, and the way you made it is the reason I am not asking for more. You tried it and reported what broke: five root files newly red, four with no front matter the parser hard-fails without, SKILL.md carrying Claude skill schema keys the parser rejects, a basis gate then demanding governing acts for each, and the examples gate executing README's shell blocks -- which are make test, make vet, make build and a network clone -- so the documentation gate would recurse into itself and acquire a network dependency CI deliberately refuses. Those files answer to external contracts. Leave them alone.\n\nTHE EXAMPLES HALF IS WITHDRAWN, not deferred. You are right that README's only runnable examples are the repository's own full gate and a public clone, so \"examples run\" cannot mean for the README what it means for a docs page, and a proxy check on make targets named in prose is exactly the wording-sensitive gate I rejected in 381c031a. I should not have written that condition; I copied the shape of a docs-page gate onto a file that is not one.\n\nSO THE SCOPE IS WHAT YOU ALREADY BUILT. The docs/why.md three-hunk de-overclaim, the matching docs/README.md hunk, and the link defect at README.md:260 -- the [architecture] shorthand with no definition, which rendered as literal brackets and which the inline-link regex could not see, now an ordinary link and therefore under the existing gate. Agreed on not gating the dangling-shorthand class: an undefined label is indistinguishable from deliberate literal brackets, and a gate that cannot tell them apart would fail on correct prose.\n\nSay in the artifact that the request which sent you looking was wrong about the gap, and that the link at 260 is a real defect you found while disproving it. A reader should not have to reconstruct that from three asserts.","body":{"area":"docs","branch":"request/readme-salvage","conditions":"Publish exact-head artifacts for the changed stable paths at the head carrying the docs/why.md de-overclaim hunks, the docs/README.md hunk, and the README.md:260 link repair, and request an independent review with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not extend the documentation walker to the repository root and do not add any gate that inspects prose wording or make-target names. Confirm in the artifact that TestLocalMarkdownLinks already covers README.md and state the evidence, including that a deliberately broken link fails it and the repair passes. Run gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 and the documentation gate with -count=1 at the exact head, and report them at that head rather than at an earlier one.","severity":"low","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}